nodecode-whoop is a rewrite of davidmosiah's davidmosiah/whoop-mcp:

  https://github.com/davidmosiah/whoop-mcp
  commit d15516fa2671e9749d43531fe0f1f447d5632686
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 David Mosiah (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the connector's read path against WHOOP's developer API v2 — the
recovery, sleep, cycle and workout collections (`/v2/recovery`,
`/v2/activity/sleep`, `/v2/cycle`, `/v2/activity/workout`) and the profile and
body measurements (`/v2/user/profile/basic`, `/v2/user/measurement/body`); the
scored-record reads (`score_state` "SCORED", the fields under `score`, the
sleep stage summary in milliseconds); the per-metric trend statistic
(average, min, max, a least-squares slope over the chronologically ordered
scored records, and the rising/falling/stable/insufficient_data direction with
the original's per-metric epsilon); the freshness rule that refreshed an
access token within 120 seconds of expiry; and the not-medical-advice posture.
Five of the connector's tools are here under their original wire names:
whoop_daily_summary, whoop_recovery_trend, whoop_sleep_trend, whoop_list_workouts
and whoop_get_profile. The Node and TypeScript — the MCP server over stdio, the
fetch and cache layers — is Common Lisp here: nlk:http for WHOOP's API and its
OAuth token endpoint, one section declaration for the settings, and
nlk:define-contract declarations for the tools' arguments, so the schema the
model is shown and the body that runs are one shape.

Left out: everything that was the MCP server rather than the data — JSON-RPC
over stdio, the local HTTP transport, the SQLite response cache, the audit and
privacy tools, the synthetic demo data, the wellness profile shared with the
author's other connectors under `~/.delx-wellness/`, and the connection-status
tool that read ~/.hermes/config.yaml. Also left out: the setup, auth and doctor
CLI commands (a cell cannot open a browser consent page for you; the README
says which command to run once), the whoop_list_* collection tools other than
workouts, and the whoop_get_cycle/get_sleep/get_workout by-id tools. The daily
summary keeps the scored values and the window averages; the original's
defensive baseline, readiness fill, diagnostics and action candidates are not
computed here.
